# Reference: values to paste into GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions
# Replace PUBLIC_IP with your VM's address (e.g. curl -fsS https://api.ipify.org).
# Defaults below match .env.docker.example (ports 5000 / 9000 / 8080 / 8888).
#
# --- Repository Secrets (recommended for credentials + URLs if you prefer one tab) ---
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI          http://PUBLIC_IP:5000
# MLFLOW_S3_ENDPOINT_URL       http://PUBLIC_IP:9000
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION           us-east-1
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID            (same as MINIO_ROOT_USER on the VM, or MINIO_ACCESS_KEY from: make minio-keys)
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY        (same as MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD on the VM, or MINIO_SECRET_KEY from: make minio-keys)
# API_HEALTH_URL               http://PUBLIC_IP:8080
# FEAST_UI_URL                 http://PUBLIC_IP:8888
#
# --- Repository Variables (optional: same NAMES; use for public URLs only. Secrets win if both are set.) ---
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI          http://PUBLIC_IP:5000
# MLFLOW_S3_ENDPOINT_URL       http://PUBLIC_IP:9000
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION           us-east-1
# API_HEALTH_URL               http://PUBLIC_IP:8080
# FEAST_UI_URL                 http://PUBLIC_IP:8888
# (Do NOT put AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY in Variables — use Secrets only.)
